=== 4. BREAK-EVEN FILL SHARE ===
  Reasoning: an unfilled order earns nothing and costs nothing. The realised edge
  per ATTEMPT is fill_share * edge_on_filled. That is positive whenever edge_on_filled
  is positive, so no fill share makes it negative -- the binding question is POWER:
  a lower fill share means fewer effective observations, so required n grows as 1/share.
  equal    observed fill=100% -> attempts needed=4070.72, days=46.46 (within 92d to Nov 6)
  equal    observed fill=64.63% -> attempts needed=6298.32, days=71.89 (within 92d to Nov 6)
  equal    observed fill=57.97% -> attempts needed=7022.17, days=80.15 (within 92d to Nov 6)
  equal    observed: fill share needed to finish by Nov 6 (92 days) = 50.5%
  equal    shrunk   fill=100% -> attempts needed=88860.1, days=1014 (BEYOND Nov 6)
  equal    shrunk   fill=64.63% -> attempts needed=137487, days=1569 (BEYOND Nov 6)
  equal    shrunk   fill=57.97% -> attempts needed=153288, days=1750 (BEYOND Nov 6)
  equal    shrunk  : fill share needed to finish by Nov 6 (92 days) = 1102%

  Sharper form: the branch stops paying off when edge on FILLED pairs <= 0.
  measured edge on filled = 0.002298043 -> positive, branch still pays
  spread cost that would zero it: 0.007298043 (currently 0.005)

